{
  "format": "astraforge-fx/1",
  "_axes": "All vectors are in the socket's Godot local axes. Godot +Y = Blender socket local +Z = 'out' (exhaust of socket_thruster_*, outward normal of turret seats, blade/shaft direction of socket_mount_hand_* and socket_grip_main, up for socket_fx_head/chest). Godot -Z = Blender socket local +Y = 'forward' of muzzles (socket_muzzle_*). Gravity is world space when local_coords is false.",
  "_fields": "amount, lifetime (s), one_shot, autostart, explosiveness, randomness, local_coords, fixed_fps (simulation Hz, default 30), direction, spread (deg), velocity [min,max] m/s, gravity m/s2, damping [min,max], tangential_accel, radial_accel, angle, angular_velocity (deg/s), scale [min,max], scale_curve [[t,v]...], color_ramp [[t,[r,g,b,a]]...], emission {shape: point|sphere|sphere_surface|box|ring, radius, inner_radius, height, axis, extents}, quad_size (m), texture: soft|spark|star|smoke|ring, blend: add|mix, turbulence, light {color, energy, range} (adds an OmniLight3D). reference_size_m (asset longest axis the preset is tuned for), reference_socket_m (seat/nozzle diameter it is tuned for). Binding params: scale (sizes and velocities), color (RGB tint), amount, lifetime, speed_scale or any field above.",
  "_scale": "Presets are metric. godot_package scales a binding without params.scale by k: socket diameter (extras diameter_m / mount_d_m / nozzle_d_m) or size_class S/M/L (representative seat 1.0/2.25/4.5 m, middle of the size-class ranges <=1.5/3/6 m; inherited from a parent socket such as a turret socket_mount) divided by reference_socket_m; else the asset's longest axis divided by reference_size_m; else 1. k multiplies every length: quad_size, velocity, damping, accelerations, gravity, emission shape, light range and visibility_aabb.",
